      "question": "A sector of 56°, cut out from a circle, contains 17.6 cm2. Find the radius of the circle",
      "options": [
        "6 cm",
        "6.5 cm",
        "5 cm",
        "5.6 cm"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 0,
      "answerSource": "derived",
      "answerKeyRef": null,
      "explanation": "Sector area is (θ/360)πr². Hence r² = 17.6 × 360/(56π). Using π = 22/7 gives r² = 36 and r = 6 cm; using a more precise π gives approximately 6 cm, matching the same option. Verified solution (unofficial); original printed paper and worked derivation checked on 26 October 2026.",
